---
---

<div class="space-y-6">
  <!-- Knowledge Header -->
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-3">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        📚 Financial Literacy & Knowledge Center
      </h2>
      <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 border border-emerald-200 uppercase tracking-wider">
        Free Education
      </span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
      Financial freedom is not about how much you earn—it is about how effectively you protect, allocate, and multiply what you keep. Master these core economic principles to accelerate your wealth.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 6 Core Knowledge Modules Grid -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
    <!-- Module 1: Compound Interest -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-xs space-y-3 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg border border-emerald-100">
        📈
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        The Rule of 72 & Compounding
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Compound interest is the eighth wonder of the world. The <strong>Rule of 72</strong> tells you how many years it takes to double your money: divide 72 by your annual return rate.
      </p>
      <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-700">
        Example: At 8% annual return (S&P 500 average), $10,000 doubles to $20,000 in exactly <strong>9 years</strong> (72 / 8 = 9).
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Module 2: Good Debt vs Bad Debt -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-xs space-y-3 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-sky-50 text-sky-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg border border-sky-100">
        ⚖️
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        Good Debt vs. Toxic Debt
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Not all debt is equal. <strong>Good debt</strong> finances assets that grow in value or produce income (e.g. low-rate mortgages, cashflowing business loans). <strong>Bad debt</strong> finances depreciating items at double-digit interest (e.g. 24% credit cards).
      </p>
      <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-700">
        Rule: If the interest rate exceeds 7%, pay it off immediately before investing in the stock market.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Module 3: Credit Scores -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-xs space-y-3 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-purple-50 text-purple-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg border border-purple-100">
        🎯
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        Credit Score Anatomy (FICO)
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        A high credit score can save you over $100,000 on mortgage and auto loan interest over your lifetime.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-[11px] text-slate-600 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
        <li><strong>35% Payment History</strong>: Never miss a due date.</li>
        <li><strong>30% Credit Utilization</strong>: Keep balances &lt; 30% of limits.</li>
        <li><strong>15% Credit Age</strong>: Keep oldest cards active.</li>
        <li><strong>10% Credit Mix & 10% New Inquiries</strong></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Module 4: Emergency Funds & HYSAs -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-xs space-y-3 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-amber-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg border border-amber-100">
        🛡️
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        Emergency Funds & High-Yield Accounts
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Traditional checking accounts pay virtually 0.01% interest. A <strong>High-Yield Savings Account (HYSA)</strong> offers 4.0%–5.0% APY while maintaining full FDIC insurance and instant liquidity.
      </p>
      <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-700">
        $10,000 in checking = $1/year. <br />
        $10,000 in a 4.5% HYSA = <strong>$450/year free interest</strong>.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Module 5: 50/30/20 Rule -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-xs space-y-3 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-teal-50 text-teal-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg border border-teal-100">
        📊
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        The 50 / 30 / 20 Budgeting Rule
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Popularized by Sen. Elizabeth Warren, this framework simplifies spending without tedious receipt micro-management:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-[11px] text-slate-600 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
        <li><strong>50% Needs</strong>: Housing, groceries, utilities, basic transit.</li>
        <li><strong>30% Wants</strong>: Dining, streaming, hobbies, travel.</li>
        <li><strong>20% Savings & Debt</strong>: Emergency fund, 401(k), extra loans.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Module 6: Inflation & Purchasing Power -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-xs space-y-3 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-rose-50 text-rose-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg border border-rose-100">
        🔥
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        Inflation & Purchasing Power
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Inflation is a silent tax on cash. At a standard 3% annual inflation rate, prices double approximately every 24 years. Holding long-term cash without investing guarantees loss of real purchasing power.
      </p>
      <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-700">
        Key: Keep only 3–6 months of expenses in cash. Invest remaining surplus into broad-market index funds (e.g. S&P 500, Total World).
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Essential Financial Glossary -->
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4">
    <div class="border-b border-slate-100 pb-3">
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        Essential Financial Terms Glossary
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-0.5">
        Clear, jargon-free definitions for every key personal finance metric.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">APR (Annual Percentage Rate)</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">The total annualized cost of borrowing money, including the base interest rate and associated lender fees.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">APY (Annual Percentage Yield)</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">The real rate of return earned on a savings account or investment over one year, taking compound interest into account.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">DTI (Debt-to-Income Ratio)</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">Your total monthly debt payments divided by your gross monthly income. Mortgage lenders typically insist on a DTI under 43%.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Net Worth</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">Everything you own (cash, investments, home equity, vehicles) minus everything you owe (mortgages, credit cards, loans).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Sinking Fund</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">A targeted savings bucket where you set aside money each month for a predictable upcoming expense (e.g. car insurance or holiday gifts).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Index Fund / ETF</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">A passive investment basket that tracks hundreds of major corporations at ultra-low expense ratios, outperforming 90% of active stock pickers.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
